Subject: tests: Coreutils.pm runs test commands with GNV bash on OpenVMS

Perl's system runs a command string with DCL, which has no shell syntax
('quoting', VAR=val, 2> redirection) and no "sed" verb, so every perl test
case failed with %DCL-W-IVVERB.  Write the command to a script and run it
with GNV bash instead.  That bash does not inherit the environment, so the
script exports PATH and the locale variables first; otherwise GNV's own,
much older sed would be tested.

--- a/testsuite/Coreutils.pm	2026-10-03 16:51:19.650085458 +0100
+++ b/testsuite/Coreutils.pm	2026-10-03 17:03:15.180648553 +0100
@@ -475,7 +475,34 @@
         }
 
       warn "Running command: '$cmd_str'\n" if $debug;
-      my $rc = 0xffff & system $cmd_str;
+      my $rc;
+      if ($^O eq 'VMS')
+        {
+          # Perl's system runs a command string with DCL, which knows no
+          # shell syntax ('quoting', VAR=val prefixes, 2> redirection).
+          # Run it with GNV bash (the DCL symbol BASH) from a script.  That
+          # bash does not inherit this environment, so the script sets the
+          # variables the tests rely on.
+          my $script = "$test_name.vms-cmd.sh";
+          open my $sh, '>', $script
+            or die "$program_name: $script: $!\n";
+          foreach my $var (qw (PATH LC_ALL LC_CTYPE LC_COLLATE LC_MESSAGES
+                               LANG LANGUAGE TMPDIR POSIXLY_CORRECT COLS))
+            {
+              print $sh "export $var=", _shell_quote ($ENV{$var}), "\n"
+                if defined $ENV{$var};
+              print $sh "unset $var\n"
+                if !defined $ENV{$var};
+            }
+          print $sh "$cmd_str\n";
+          close $sh;
+          $rc = 0xffff & system "bash $script";
+          unlink $script;
+        }
+      else
+        {
+          $rc = 0xffff & system $cmd_str;
+        }
 
       # Restore any environment setting we changed via a deletion.
       foreach my $env_sym (keys %pushed_env)
